quran[5]{c,v,t}:
  57,25,"Indeed, We sent Our messengers with clear proofs, and We sent down the Book and the Balance with them so that people could uphold justice. And We sent down iron, in which there is great might and benefits for humanity. So that Allah may make known those who help Him and His messengers without seeing (Him). Indeed, Allah is All-Strong, All-Mighty."
  57,26,"Indeed, We sent Nuh (Noah) and Ibrahim (Abraham) and established prophethood and the Book among their descendants. Some of them are rightly guided, yet many of them are transgressors."
  57,27,"Then We followed them up with Our messengers, and afterwards We sent ‘Isa, son of Maryam (Jesus, son of Mary), and We gave him the Injil (the Gospel). And We instilled kindness and mercy into the hearts of those who followed him. As for monasticism, they innovated it (themselves). We did not ordain it for them, but (they invented it) only to seek Allah’s pleasure. Yet they did not observe it with proper observance. So We gave to the believers among them their (due) reward. But many of them are transgressors."
  57,28,"O believers! Be God-conscious and have faith in His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him). He will grant you a double share of His mercy, provide light to help you walk (in this world and the Hereafter) and forgive you. Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  57,29,So that the People of the Book may know that they have no power over anything of Allah’s grace and that (all) grace is in Allah’s Hand. He grants it to whomever He pleases. And Allah is the Possessor of Tremendous Grace.
